</div><p id="import-auto-id2688907">One mole of a nuclide <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0"> size 12{"" lSup { size 8{A} } X} {}</annotation></semantics></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> has a mass of <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0"> size 12{A} {}</annotation></semantics></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> grams, so that one mole of <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>137</mtext></msup><mtext>Cs</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>137</mtext></msup><mtext>Cs</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0"> size 12{"" lSup { size 8{"137"} } "Cs"} {}</annotation></semantics></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> has a mass of 137 g. A mole has <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mrow><mtext>02 </mtext><mo stretchy="false">×</mo><msup><mtext>10</mtext><mrow><mtext>23</mtext></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mrow><mtext>02 </mtext><mo stretchy="false">×</mo><msup><mtext>10</mtext><mrow><mtext>23</mtext></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0"> size 12{6 "." "02 " times "10" rSup { size 8{"23"} } } {}</annotation></semantics></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> nuclei. Thus the mass of <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>137</mtext></msup><mtext>Cs</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>137</mtext></msup><mtext>Cs</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0"> size 12{"" lSup { size 8{"137"} } "Cs"} {}</annotation></semantics></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> released was</p><div data-type="equation" id="eip-187"><math display="block"><semantics><mrow>
